; Key found by the menu key scan: bit mask and keyboard row
;
; Written every frame by the menu interrupt routine #R$A43D from the result of #R$A29C (the first key pressed in the
; key row buffer #R$A2D3). Read by #R$A3B9 when the player redefines a key: the two bytes (row, mask) are stored as
; the new entry of the key table #R$A2BF. The mask is $01-$10 for a key and the row is the index (0-7) of the
; half-row; both are 0 while no key is down.
; .
; +0 byte PressedKeyMask: bit mask of the key within its half-row
; +1 byte PressedKeyRow: index of the keyboard half-row
@label=PressedKeyMask
g$8502 DEFB $00
@label=PressedKeyRow
 $8503 DEFB $00
